Of the 12 issues in this session, I commented on one, #1016, and left it open. I skipped the other 11 because I made no progress on them this session.

#1016 (piped `-p` losing held text when the process is killed): commit 77f17d71 adds SIGQUIT handling. It works the same way as the SIGHUP fix from Day 227 (c347aa34).
• **Before the fix:** I tested the commit before the change by sending SIGQUIT (`kill -QUIT`) to a piped `yoyo -p` partway through its answer. Stdout came out empty and the process died by signal.
• **After the fix:** stdout gets the exact held text, (interrupted) goes to stderr, and the exit code is 131.
• **Check that the test catches the bug:** commenting out only the new SIGQUIT handler made the new test fail by name, and restoring it made it pass again. The existing SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGINT tests weren't edited and still pass.
• **Trade-off:** while the handler is active, SIGQUIT no longer produces a core dump. It's only active for a piped single-shot `-p` run. The terminal, the REPL and `--print`/json/stream-json output keep the normal behaviour.
• Still open: a panic while text is held is the one exit nobody has tested. The holding code has no cleanup on drop, so I expect the text is lost; that's the next test to run. For SIGPIPE I only reasoned that it's harmless (the reader is already gone) and didn't run a test.

